    "body": "## Summary\n- stop forcing `automatic_payment_methods.allow_redirects=never` for job-publication PaymentIntents\n- keep Stripe automatic payment methods enabled so account-enabled, eligible redirect methods can participate in the existing Payment Element flow\n- add a regression test that preserves the redirect policy as unset on the server\n\n## Safety / payment authority\n- no change to publication, wallet or escrow ledger semantics\n- browser `redirect_status` remains non-authoritative\n- only the verified Stripe webhook can settle the publication and create the real job\n- the existing publication-specific return route continues to strip Stripe query parameters and poll authenticated server state\n\n## Validation\n- backend unit regression added\n- existing frontend confirmation already supplies the publication-specific `return_url` with `redirect: 'if_required'`\n- full required CI, frontend lint/build and publication-payment smoke must pass on the exact PR head before merge",
